    "options": {
      "A": "Use $c=\\sqrt{6^2+8^2}$ even if the triangle is not right-angled and $c$ is not the hypotenuse, skipping those conditions.",
      "B": "Find a missing leg by adding the known squares the same way, as when the unknown is a leg rather than the hypotenuse.",
      "C": "Rearrange to $c=\\sqrt{a^2+b^2}=\\sqrt{36+64}=\\sqrt{100}=10$, taking the positive square root.",
      "D": "Compute $c=6^2+8^2=100$ and stop, leaving the value squared instead of taking the positive square root."
    },
